## Port of pumpkin/src/entity/player.rs
## Port of pumpkin/src/entity/living.rs
## Port of pumpkin/src/entity/hunger.rs: the data only; `tick` and `eat` are entity/hunger.aowl.
## PARTIAL: pumpkin/src/entity/player.rs - the player a client plays as: `ChunkManager`, `Abilities`, chat sessions, health and hunger, mining, screen handlers (`open_handled_screen` is here, Java half), gamemode, NBT, `impl InventoryPlayer`, statistics (`gPlayerStats`, kept in the player's NBT as upstream does), `set_respawn_point`, `drop_item` and `increment_stat` through hooks. `attack` is entity/playerattack.aowl, `calculate_respawn_point` is entity/respawn.aowl, item cooldowns are item/itembehaviour.aowl, `tick_maps` is world/mapglue.aowl, `send_effect`, `tick_experience`, `set_tab_list_header_footer` and the like are entity/playerextras.aowl, damage, death, wake up (with the bed's `occupied` reset), breath and the hunger tick are block/worldhooks.aowl, the night skip and the cross-dimension `respawn_player` are world/worldmod.aowl. `update_player_pose`, `can_fit_pose`, the camera target follow and `get_movement_statistic` (counted by net/java/play.aowl's `afterMove`) are entity/playerextras.aowl, `open_handled_screen_direct` is here, the item in use is the `LivingEntity`'s (`set_active_hand`; `start_using_item` and friends are its `item_in_use`), and the `Entity`/`LivingEntity` NBT halves (fire, air, effects) go through `gPlayerLivingWriteHook`. `get_mining_speed` has haste, conduit power and mining fatigue (entitymod sets `gMiningEffectsHook`). Still missing: the Bedrock halves, a player's bounding box and eye height stay the standing ones (entitymod's `syncFromPlayer`), so a crouching or swimming pose changes the metadata only, particles and sounds of a few calls, `PlayerChangeWorldEvent` and `PlayerRespawnEvent`, and portals (`teleport_world` is only the half a respawn needs).
## PARTIAL: pumpkin/src/entity/living.rs - what a player reads of it: health, absorption, `fall` (with its damage through block/worldhooks.aowl), `send_equipment_changes`, NBT. `LivingEntity::tick` runs for a player as the entity tick, block collisions, effects and the hurt cooldown, not `tick_movement`.
##
## The types are in ../serverbase.aowl. Everything sent here goes through the client's single outgoing buffer, so
## upstream's `send_packet_now` and `enqueue_packet` are the same call.

{.feature: "untyped".}

